# ---- sea wall: an unlit teal plane 5 m behind the action, from the water line down, on a one-colour
# ramp (the same teal as the sky's lower half, so it is invisible): it hides the sun as it sets and the
# islet's foot below the water line.
open("seawall.txt", "w").write(f"""# Sea wall: an unlit teal plane 18 x 6.6 m facing the camera, its top at the water line, 5 m back.
# Generated by make_env.py.
new
{mat("Sea", "teal", True)}
add mesh grid --name Wall --x-subdivisions 2 --y-subdivisions 2 --size 1 --location 0 5 -3.3 --rotation 90 0 0
scale 18 1 6.6
apply --scale
material assign Sea
shade flat
export seawall.glb
""")
